 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S446-014\", \"clauses\": {\"multiply_numbers\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} × {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F16 prints a multiplication question whose two factors come from the a and b domains; every render is a find-the-product task, matching the declared task_type find_product and structure result_unknown.\"}, \"with_and_without_regrouping\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} × {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The a runs include both two-digit and three-digit values and the b runs include one-digit values, so F16 produces products that need regrouping and products that do not, across renders.\"}, \"2_to_3_digit_by_1_digit\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} × {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The a runs include two-digit and three-digit values (10 to 11, 19, 21, ... 999 range observed) and the b runs include one-digit values 2 to 3 and 5 to 10, so two- or three-digit numbers multiplied by a one-digit number are produced.\"}, \"2_to_4_digit_by_leading_non_zero\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} × {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The b runs include 30, 40, 50 ... 900, whose leading digit is the only non-zero digit, and the a runs include 1000, a four-digit number, so two- to four-digit numbers multiplied by such a number are produced.\"}, \"products_up_to_10_000\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} × {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"declared_bounds sets max_product to 10000 for this lc with table one_digit_or_leading_digit, so every F16 problem's product is held at or below 10000; the result runs of F07 also reach 10000.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F04\", \"F05\", \"F06\", \"F17\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Think of it as {b} {count_noun}: {groups}.\", \"Use the {b} times table: {b} × {a}.\", \"We need to {mul_phrase} {b} {count_noun}.\", \"{a} × {b} = {fill_value}\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F04 and F06: the count_noun domain offers singular forms (group of N) alongside plural forms (groups of N) with no tie to a count of one; F06's template_chosen_by_values is empty and F04's b printed runs are 2 to 5, so a singular noun after a count of 2 or more is producible, which is wrong agreement in learner-facing hints. F05: the phrase times table is not in cumulative_vocab, and the b domain prints 20 to 900 (for example 900 itself), so the hint asks a grade 3 learner to use a times table for a three-digit number, a concept beyond this lc's scope. F17: the fill_value distractor list (distractors shaped like the keyed answer) includes 80, the a runs include 10 and the b runs include 8, so the statement 10 × 8 = 80 can print as a true statement drawn from the false-keyed distractor set; the domains do not exclude a distractor equal to the product, so a keyed-false True or False item can be wrong. Not judged here: F03's tens_a and ones_a are arithmetic values whose correctness the reason_kinds entry assigns to the hint contract (§16) and §1E, so no finding is made on them.\"}",
